SOCIO-PROFESSIONAL TEST FOR HOTELERY-INTENDENCE MANAGEMENT (90%), 50% to 60%
Deployed at several sites, the Lavigny Institution consists of a neurological hospital with outpatient consultations at two sites, a housing department for adults with disabilities, intellectual disability or physical problems, a specialized school and a socio-professional department.

In order to strengthen our team on our Lavigny site, we are looking for an e :

SOCIOPROFESSIONAL TEST FOR HOTELERIAN-INTENDENCE MANAGEMENT (90%)

The socio-professional department of our institution is a partner of the FORJAD programme, initiated by the Canton of Vaud, which allows young adults to acquire certification training (AFP/CFC) while developing their professional skills.
Your Mission
You accompany young adults in their training journey by transmitting the technical and professional skills of the stewardship manager trade. Every day, you contribute to their development while guaranteeing quality services within our institution.
Your main responsibilities

• Manage and lead the Stewardship workshop, ensuring the progressive acquisition of competencies according to the AFP/CFC training plans.

• Train, support and evaluate trainees and apprentices in their career paths.

• Coordinate and monitor apprenticeships carried out in the various sectors of the institution, in close cooperation with other trainers.

• Plan, organize and participate in the daily maintenance activities of the departmental premises.

• Ensure the quality of stewardship services and compliance with hygiene, safety and organizational standards.

• Actively participate in interdisciplinary collaboration that promotes the success of trainees and the smooth functioning of the department.
Your profile
You enjoy passing on your know-how and accompanying young adults in their professional development. Organised, autonomous and endowed with an excellent relational sense, you know how to combine professional requirements and benevolent support.
You hold:

• An SWC of stewardship manager, with at least 5 years of professional experience ideally complemented by a federal patent;

• A diploma of socio-professional teachership (MSP);

• A certification of trainer in company (FEE).
You also have:

• Strong organizational, adaptation and autonomy capacities;

• An excellent sense of responsibility and planning;

• Good pedagogical, relational and communication skills;

• An ease in working in a multidisciplinary team;

• Good editorial skills and excellent mastery of common computer tools;

• A valid driving licence (category B) and a vehicle.

• A varied and stimulating position within an institution recognized and committed to a meaningful mission;

• The opportunity to contribute to the training and vocational integration of young adults;

• A pleasant, collaborative and caring working environment within dynamic and motivated teams;

• Opportunities for professional development through internal and external training;

• Wage conditions according to the CLC of the public social sector of voodoo;

• Attractive social benefits: business restaurant, free parking or shuttles from Morges station.
We offer you
We offer you

• A varied and stimulating position within a human and caring environment;

• The opportunity to contribute to a meaningful social mission;

• Working conditions in accordance with the Convention on the Rights of the Child;

• Opportunities for professional and personal development;

• A business restaurant at preferential rates;

• Free parking is available.

Entry into office: 1 November 2026 or date to be agreed
Contact: Pierre-André Cusin, Director of the Tel. 021.821.45.45

If you want to put your skills at the service of an institutional project rich in human values, it is with pleasure that we await your complete application file (motivation letter, CV, copies of diplomas and work certificates).

